00:48:09,100 --> 00:48:12,100
要是显示25，就得立马下车。
If it says 25,
we've got to jump off.

676
00:48:12,100 --> 00:48:15,100
23…
23...

677
00:48:17,540 --> 00:48:20,340
是的。是的！
Yes. Yes!

678
00:48:20,340 --> 00:48:21,700
我居然没慌！（）
I didn't panic(!)

679
00:48:23,260 --> 00:48:26,700
这就是没有拥堵费的下场。
This is what comes of not
having a congestion charge.

680
00:48:39,220 --> 00:48:43,780
我们又站在另一站，找去久里滨的列车。
We were now at yet another station
looking for the train to Kurihama.

681
00:48:43,780 --> 00:48:45,900
黑滨？黑滨？
Kurihama? Kurihama?

682
00:48:45,900 --> 00:48:47,540
黑滨？
Kurihama?

683
00:48:49,580 --> 00:48:53,260
我本来胸有成竹，结果偶尔在红灯前卡住时，
I was so confident that
when I did occasionally
get stuck at the lights,

684
00:48:53,260 --> 00:48:57,500
我只好掏出办公室里那帮日系玩具来救场。
I broke out some of the Japanese
toys the office had provided.

685
00:48:57,500 --> 00:48:57,540
玩具吉他演奏
TOY GUITAR PLAYS

686
00:48:57,580 --> 00:48:59,180
这玩意儿是空气吉他！
It's an air guitar!

687
00:49:09,980 --> 00:49:14,220
手机响起——是梅还是哈蒙德。
MOBILE RINGS
It's May or Hammond.

688
00:49:14,220 --> 00:49:18,220
喂，杰里米。哈蒙德，你怎么样？我很好，
Hello. Jeremy. Hammond, how are you?
I'm very well,

689
00:49:18,220 --> 00:49:19,620
你呢？
how are you doing?

690
00:49:19,620 --> 00:49:24,380
我现在在东京，一切顺利，我去看看导航。
I am in Tokyo, and I'm
going brilliantly well,
I shall look on my sat nav.

691
00:49:24,380 --> 00:49:26,140
‘你开了多快？’
'How fast are you going?'

692
00:49:27,820 --> 00:49:32,060
我的天啊，什么？我刚把导航……
Oh, my God. What?
I've just turned the sat...

693
00:49:32,060 --> 00:49:33,780
关掉了导航。
I've turned the sat nav off.

694
00:49:33,780 --> 00:49:36,060
你干嘛关了它？
Why did you do that?

695
00:49:36,060 --> 00:49:41,100
我只是想看看自己在哪儿，因为开着的时候手机上会显示。
I just wanted to look where I was,
cos it comes up on
the phone thing when you're on.

696
00:49:41,100 --> 00:49:45,740
好啊，我现在可以精确告诉你你在哪儿——导航关了，你迷路了！拜！
Well, I can tell you exactly
where you are now you've
turned your sat nav off. Lost! Bye!

697
00:49:45,740 --> 00:49:52,700
导航全是日文，我根本不知道怎么重新开。
With all the sat nav's controls
in Japanese, I had no clue
how to get it back on again.

698
00:49:52,700 --> 00:49:55,060
哦，这简直……
Oh, this is just...

699
00:49:55,060 --> 00:49:56,460
我得……
I'm going to have to...

700
00:49:59,260 --> 00:50:01,140
这可是个好时刻。
This was a good moment.

701
00:50:01,140 --> 00:50:06,820
我们成功赶上了四辆火车的最后一辆，离终点还有两小时。
We had successfully caught the last
of our four trains and would be
at the finish line in two hours.

702
00:50:06,820 --> 00:50:10,340
与此同时，杰里米竟然第一次出乱子。
Meanwhile, Jeremy,
for the first time, was in trouble.

703
00:50:13,380 --> 00:50:15,380
不。
No.

704
00:50:18,460 --> 00:50:24,500
对，有架飞机要在那儿降落，那应该是……成田机场就在那边。
Right, there's a plane coming in
to land there, that must
mean...Narita airport's over there.

705
00:50:27,100 --> 00:50:31,100
翻译员说日语：抱歉，我刚才只问了酒单。
TRANSLATOR SPEAKS JAPANESE
Sorry, I just asked for
the wine list.

706
00:50:31,100 --> 00:50:36,140
这不对。奇怪的是，我居然找到了会说英语的警察。
That's not right. Amazingly, I
found a policeman who spoke English.

707
00:50:36,140 --> 00:50:38,100
‘算吧。’是的，这条隧道。
'Sort of.' Yes, this tunnel.

708
00:50:38,100 --> 00:50:41,700
这条路会往下走，呃……
This road will lead down, uh...

709
00:50:41,700 --> 00:50:45,860
一、二、三……四信号。
one, two, three...four signal.

710
00:50:45,860 --> 00:50:48,540
灯光？也就是四个信号？
Lights? So four signals?

711
00:50:48,540 --> 00:50:51,220
四个吧，也许？
Four, maybe. Maybe?

712
00:50:51,220 --> 00:50:58,420
等火车在站里，我们上了车，我去试试车上的饮料机运气。
As our train waited in the station,
I went to try my luck with one
of the onboard drinks machines.

713
00:50:58,420 --> 00:51:01,180
手机响起——接着詹姆斯打来。
MOBILE RINGS
Then James rang.

714
00:51:01,180 --> 00:51:05,500
喂？好的，我会的。我还没找到自动贩卖机，找到就买。
Hello? Yeah, will do. I haven't
found a vending machine yet,
but as soon as I do, I will.

715
00:51:05,500 --> 00:51:07,660
嗯，但我们根本没动。
Yeah, but we're not moving.

716
00:51:09,700 --> 00:51:11,260
好吧，现在确实没动。
Well, not now we're not.

717
00:51:12,980 --> 00:51:15,500
你说我们在动？不，我们没动。
What do you mean we are?
No, we're not.

718
00:51:17,900 --> 00:51:19,940
兄弟，我根本不在——
Mate, I'm not on the...

719
00:51:19,940 --> 00:51:21,140
我怎么会不——？
How can I not...?

720
00:51:22,300 --> 00:51:26,260
档位、刹车、加速。
Gear position,
braking, acceleration.

721
00:51:28,740 --> 00:51:30,740
手机铃声
你好。
MOBILE RINGS
Hello.

722
00:51:30,740 --> 00:51:35,940
詹姆斯？不，是我，不是詹姆斯……詹姆斯怎么会给你打电话？
James? No, it's not James,
it's me... Why would James
be ringing you up?

723
00:51:37,860 --> 00:51:40,140
因为有……
Because there's...

724
00:51:40,140 --> 00:51:42,340
有点奇怪的事儿发生了。
Something peculiar has happened.

725
00:51:42,340 --> 00:51:45,340
我们不是同一趟火车上。
We're not on the same train.

726
00:51:45,340 --> 00:51:47,100
什么？！嗨。
What?! Hello.

727
00:51:47,100 --> 00:51:49,660
我们不是同一趟火车上。
We're not on the same train.

728
00:51:49,660 --> 00:51:54,700
火车在站里停了，我就在旁边走，想去自动售货机找点喝的，
The train stopped in a station,
I was walking along it to try and
find some drinks from a machine,

729
00:51:54,700 --> 00:51:58,620
结果詹姆斯走到前面去了，火车前后分离，
and then James had moved off, he was
in the front of the train, it split,

730
00:51:58,620 --> 00:52:01,060
我还不知道在哪儿。
I don't know where yet.

731
00:52:01,060 --> 00:52:06,540
我在站里停下，跳下车去看看发生了什么，结果我的车自己跑走了。
I stopped in the station, then
I got off my train to see what had
happened, and then my train left.

732
00:52:06,540 --> 00:52:09,100
所以如果那是对的那趟车，我根本不在上面。
So if that was the right train,
I'm not on it.

733
00:52:09,100 --> 00:52:13,020
要是那不是对的……我们俩里有一个在正确的车上，一个不在。
If it wasn't the right...
One of us is on the right train,
one of us isn't.

734
00:52:13,020 --> 00:52:16,380
安慰一下吧，兄弟，我刚到个死胡同。
If it's any consolation, mate,
I've just arrived at a dead end.

735
00:52:16,380 --> 00:52:20,380
我得赶紧给詹姆斯打电话，抱歉。
I've got to ring James now,
I'm sorry.

736
00:52:20,380 --> 00:52:23,660
我可能就凭这事去买杯咖啡吧，哈哈哈！
I might just go for a cup of coffee
on this basis. Ha-ha-ha!

737
00:52:25,660 --> 00:52:29,260
‘我现在正一个人，只有个《女巫布莱尔》手持摄像机。’
'I was just now all alone with just
a Blair Witch Handycam.'

738
00:52:31,260 --> 00:52:32,900
各位观众，大家好。
Hello, viewers.

739
00:52:32,900 --> 00:52:38,620
Jezzer显然和哈蒙德聊过了，因为他刚打给我炫耀。
Jezzer has obviously
spoken to Hammond, because Jezzer's
just rung me up to gloat.

740
00:52:40,020 --> 00:52:42,020
呃……黑滨？
Erm... Kurihama?

741
00:52:42,020 --> 00:52:43,500
黑滨，没错。
Kurihama, yeah.

742
00:52:43,500 --> 00:52:45,900
好的，请稍等。下来吧。
OK, moment, please. Come down.

743
00:52:45,900 --> 00:52:50,300
这家伙让我上了正确的车，我给詹姆斯打了电话。
This man got me on the
right train, and I called James.

744
00:52:58,060 --> 00:53:04,820
但我的车比詹姆斯的晚了15分钟，我剩不到两分钟赶公交。
But my train was 15 minutes behind
James's, so I'd have less than
two minutes to catch the bus.

745
00:53:04,820 --> 00:53:07,460
你得忍住。
You're going to have to hold it.

746
00:53:07,460 --> 00:53:11,860
赶紧拼命跑去追公交，错过就完蛋了。
Just run like hell from the bus,
because if you miss
the bus, we're stuffed.

747
00:53:15,900 --> 00:53:20,100
导航说日语，艾米回来了！艾米回来了！
SAT NAV SPEAKS IN JAPANESE
Amy's back! Amy's back!

748
00:53:20,100 --> 00:53:22,020
艾米又出现在我的画面上！
Amy's back on my screen!

749
00:53:22,020 --> 00:53:24,780
我全开，艾米回来了！
I pushed everything, she's back!

750
00:53:24,780 --> 00:53:28,900
而且还没来得及—迷路让我耽误了45分钟。
And not before time - being
lost had cost me 45 minutes.

751
00:53:28,900 --> 00:53:32,420
我积的领先全被抹平了。
The lead I built up
had been wiped out.

752
00:53:32,420 --> 00:53:36,060
给我来点马力，车子，给我秀秀你的肌肉。
Show me some of your muscles,
car, show me your muscles.

753
00:53:37,860 --> 00:53:41,020
翻译器在说日语
TRANSLATOR SPEAKS JAPANESE

754
00:53:41,020 --> 00:53:43,220
那句是‘你认识我的朋友吗？’
That says, "Do you know my friend?"

755
00:53:43,220 --> 00:53:46,300
我的意思是‘请稍等一下’。
I mean, "Can you wait, please?"

756
00:53:46,300 --> 00:53:52,100
‘我现在已经下了车，祈祷詹姆斯已经拦住了公交。’
'I was now off the train and hoping
to God James had held the bus.'

757
00:53:52,100 --> 00:53:54,540
公交，应该有的呀。可是一辆也没有。
Buses, there should be buses.
There's no buses.

758
00:53:58,420 --> 00:54:02,780
我现在急冲冲往海湾下面的隧道跑去，
I was now heading for the tunnel
under the bay in a big hurry,

759
00:54:02,780 --> 00:54:06,700
GT-R第一次真的活了起来。
and for the first time
the GT-R was starting to come alive.

760
00:54:06,700 --> 00:54:12,540
你这么踩油门，简直只能嗅到最淡的味道。
When you put your foot down like
that, you just get the vaguest whiff

761
00:54:12,540 --> 00:54:16,260
这车居然能在纽博格林跑个7分29秒。
that this car can go round the
Nurburgring in 7 minutes 29 seconds.

762
00:54:16,260 --> 00:54:21,500
比麦克拉伦‑奔驰还快，比911 Turbo还快。
That's faster than
a McLaren Mercedes,
it's faster than a 911 Turbo.

763
00:54:23,460 --> 00:54:25,460
手机响起  
喂？May。
MOBILE RINGS
Hello? May.

764
00:54:25,460 --> 00:54:29,740
我和老搭档理查德·哈蒙德在一起。（该死！）哦，太好了！
I'm with my old mate Richard Hammond.
(Damn it!) Oh, great!

765
00:54:29,740 --> 00:54:32,460
兄弟，他们要抓你，因为你在玩手机。
Mate, they're cross
cos you're on your mobile.

766
00:54:32,460 --> 00:54:35,820
喂？我们现在因为在公交上打电话闹麻烦了。
Hello? We're in trouble now for
talking on a phone on the bus.

767
00:54:35,820 --> 00:54:38,700
他想跟你说话。
He wants to talk to you.

768
00:54:38,700 --> 00:54:42,900
哦…嗨。你知道你到底什么时候上那船吗？
Oh... Hi.
Do you know what time you're
actually getting on that ferry?

769
00:54:42,900 --> 00:54:47,020
25分发船，我们大概22分上船。
25 past, it leaves, we're getting
on it at about 22 minutes past.

770
00:54:48,020 --> 00:54:51,620
我们现在离海湾只有几分钟路程。
All of us were now
minutes from the bay.

771
00:54:54,940 --> 00:54:57,300
铃声不行吗？
Is that bell bad?

772
00:55:04,620 --> 00:55:06,020
现在真的很近了。
This is really close now.

773
00:55:07,860 --> 00:55:11,460
仍然套在日本公共交通的怀抱里，
Still in the bosom of
Japanese public transport,

774
00:55:11,460 --> 00:55:16,100
55分钟后到达终点。
the finish line in 55 minutes.

775
00:55:16,100 --> 00:55:20,260
我们只能祈祷杰里米的命运更不可预测。
All we could do was hope Jeremy's
life would be less predictable.

776
00:55:20,260 --> 00:55:21,900
这要看……有多忙。
It depends... How busy it is.

777
00:55:21,900 --> 00:55:27,420
……地形如何，路是否狭窄，是否车流多，是否有限速，
..on the terrain, whether it's
small roads, whether it's busy,
whether there's a speed limit,

778
00:55:27,420 --> 00:55:29,940
以及他会不会迷路。
whether he gets lost.

779
00:55:29,940 --> 00:55:34,380
狭窄道路？倒也不算。
Small roads? No, not really.

780
00:55:48,420 --> 00:55:54,420
当那座宏伟的大桥结束时，我就知道全靠最后冲上山的那一段了。
As the immense bridge ended,
I knew it would all be down to
the final charge up the mountain.

781
00:55:54,420 --> 00:56:01,580
说实话，我想赢这局现在只能靠神风了，我正好有办法。
Frankly, what I'm going to need
to win this now is a divine wind,
and I've got just the thing.

782
00:56:01,580 --> 00:56:04,980
我准备好了！冲啊！
I'm ready! Here we go!

783
00:56:09,980 --> 00:56:15,220
我早就知道他们会在4点25分正好到终点。
I knew they'd be at the finish line
at 4.25 precisely.

784
00:56:15,220 --> 00:56:18,260
抵达时间，4点31分。
Arrival time, 4.31.

785
00:56:18,260 --> 00:56:20,180
比他们晚了整整六分钟。
That's six minutes after them.

786
00:56:23,220 --> 00:56:26,460
我把变速箱调到赛模式，这样换挡更快。
I'm putting the gear box in race,
that speeds up the change time.

787
00:56:26,460 --> 00:56:29,700
我要把悬挂调到赛模式，让车子更硬。
I'm going to put the suspension in
race, that firms it right up.

788
00:56:29,700 --> 00:56:34,060
接着把牵引控制调到赛模式，让我还能打点滑。
Then I'm going to put
the traction control in race,
that lets me have some slip.

789
00:56:34,060 --> 00:56:41,580
准时到达，渡轮靠岸，离缆车整整一英里，但我们根本不打算走路。
Bang on time, the ferry docked,
a full mile from the cable car,
but we had no intention of walking.

790
00:56:48,100 --> 00:56:51,500
我没时间为了这些栏杆减速。
I've no time to slow down
for these barriers.

791
00:56:51,500 --> 00:56:55,580
就像在温布尔顿，手臂上挂着那种栏杆。
Wimbledon with barriers
like that on the end of your arm.

792
00:56:58,180 --> 00:57:01,980
我前方是一条山路——GT‑R的天下。
Ahead of me lay the mountain road -
GT-R country.

793
00:57:04,740 --> 00:57:11,700
天啊……现在一切都融合了，这不就是一辆GT‑R吗。
God...
Just now it's all coming together,
it's all just becoming a GT-R.

794
00:57:13,220 --> 00:57:17,820
“喂”。杰里米。是啊，你在哪儿？
'Hello.' Jeremy. Yeah,
where are you?

795
00:57:17,820 --> 00:57:19,780
我们现在正在下船。
We are disembarking now.

796
00:57:19,780 --> 00:57:23,580
这简直太他妈近了。
This is so damn close.

797
00:57:23,580 --> 00:57:28,820
我算不出来，但他……他……离得很近。
I can't work it out,
but he is...he is...very close.

798
00:57:28,820 --> 00:57:31,860
我现在把时间算到4点27分。
I've now got it down to 4.27.

799
00:57:31,860 --> 00:57:34,460
准备好了吗？好。
Ready? Yes.

800
00:57:34,460 --> 00:57:35,660
那就上。走起。
Let's do it. Right.

801
00:57:42,380 --> 00:57:44,580
呃！哇！啊！
Uh! Wah! Ah!

802
00:57:44,580 --> 00:57:46,060
啊！
Ah!

803
00:57:50,580 --> 00:57:53,100
4.24。
4.24.

804
00:57:53,100 --> 00:57:57,620
这可是泰坦之战，又一次要把胜负绞到最后一秒。
This is the clash
of the titans now, and it's
going down to the wire again.

805
00:58:02,460 --> 00:58:05,940
哦，不不不不不！
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

806
00:58:14,420 --> 00:58:17,260
真希望你们能感受到我现在的心跳。
I wish you could feel
my heart rate now.

807
00:58:17,260 --> 00:58:21,060
真的想让你们体会到现场到底有多疯狂。
I really wish you could
feel what's going on here.

808
00:58:21,060 --> 00:58:22,660
冲啊！
Go!

809
00:58:26,340 --> 00:58:29,580
等等啊！谢谢。
Hold on! Thank you.

810
00:58:31,940 --> 00:58:37,780
来啊来啊来啊，宝贝！“我已经把所有都倾注进去。”
Come on, come on, come on, baby!
'I was now giving it everything.'

811
00:58:39,820 --> 00:58:42,740
于是这里的山顶上有一尊佛像
So at the top here there is a Buddha

812
00:58:42,740 --> 00:58:45,340
跟道路安全有关，显然。
to road safety. Apparently.

813
00:58:45,340 --> 00:58:50,420
要是我们到了，杰里米的 GT‑R 掉进佛像里，那不是太妙了？
Wouldn't it be brilliant if
we got there and Jeremy's GT-R
was buried in the middle of it?

814
00:58:50,420 --> 00:58:53,020
“看我的，我来了…” “哎呀。” “砰。”
"Watch this, I'm here..."
"Oh, dear." "Bang."

815
00:58:56,620 --> 00:58:59,140
谢谢，谢谢，谢谢。
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

816
00:59:02,700 --> 00:59:06,860
这边走。总算抵达佛像的停车场了。
This way. Finally, I made it
to to the Buddha's car park.

817
00:59:06,860 --> 00:59:09,100
胜利属于我！
Victory is mine!

818
00:59:09,100 --> 00:59:10,780
但那根本不是终点线。
But that wasn't the finishing line.

819
00:59:10,780 --> 00:59:13,580
跑哪儿去？哪儿？
Go where? Where?

820
00:59:13,580 --> 00:59:17,340
跑啊！快啊，快快快！别管它，别管它，别管它！
Run! Come on, go, go, go!
Just leave it, leave it, leave it!

821
00:59:17,340 --> 00:59:18,660
那不是庙啊。
That's not a temple.

822
00:59:18,660 --> 00:59:22,980
我们现在从两条不同的路向佛像汇聚。
We were now converging on
the Buddha up two different paths.

823
00:59:22,980 --> 00:59:27,060
你确定没 overshoot（冲过）它吗？快点！
Are you sure we haven't overshot it?
Come on!

824
00:59:29,220 --> 00:59:30,780
不！
No!

825
00:59:39,580 --> 00:59:42,420
求求你，老天...别让他们到这儿来。
Please, God...
don't let them be here.

826
00:59:42,420 --> 00:59:45,460
他喘得像发动机一样
HE PANTS HEAVILY

827
00:59:50,780 --> 00:59:52,260
他们不在这儿。
They aren't here.

828
00:59:58,860 --> 01:00:00,660
一辆车刚刚甩掉子弹列车。
A car just beat the Bullet Train.

829
01:00:06,180 --> 01:00:08,820
那是佛像！这可是‘佛像护路’！
That's Buddha!
This is the Buddha to road safety!

830
01:00:08,820 --> 01:00:15,980
这堵墙是 12 世纪的，呃……记得我刚才给你们的讲座吧……
And this wall was 12th century,
erm...so you remember from
the lecture I was giving you...

831
01:00:15,980 --> 01:00:17,780
嗨，各位！哦。
Hi, guys! Oh.

832
01:00:17,780 --> 01:00:21,740
有意思……这和那边的世纪不一样。
Just interesting...how this
is a different century to that.

833
01:00:21,740 --> 01:00:24,260
是啊。是啊。
Yeah. Yeah.

834
01:00:24,260 --> 01:00:28,020
你们也冲上去了？哦，是啊。
You ran up there as well? Oh, yeah.

835
01:00:28,020 --> 01:00:30,140
恭喜啊。
Congratulations.

836
01:00:30,140 --> 01:00:32,820
你们在这儿多久了？真的不久。
How long have you been here?
Really not long.

837
01:00:32,820 --> 01:00:34,700
真的？说实话？
Genuinely? Honestly?

838
01:00:34,700 --> 01:00:38,540
三分零十二秒。
Three minutes 12 seconds.

839
01:00:38,540 --> 01:00:41,140
这么接近。
That is so close.

840
01:00:41,140 --> 01:00:43,660
谢谢，佛像。你帮他盯着了。
Thanks, Buddha.
You looked after him.

841
01:00:43,660 --> 01:00:46,900
失望啊！等着看！
Disappointed! Wait for it.

842
01:00:46,900 --> 01:00:51,460
译者说日语
是哪种？那就是日语…
怎么了？“哦，鸡巴！”
TRANSLATOR SPEAKS JAPANESE
Which is? That's the Japanese...
For? "Oh, cock!"

843
01:01:12,220 --> 01:01:13,860
现在，看——
Now, look,

844
01:01:13,860 --> 01:01:17,980
我们安排这些比赛，就是想让它们够贴近，尽管如此。
we do arrange those races so that
we know they're going to be
close, but even so.

845
01:01:17,980 --> 01:01:23,140
这真是太惊人了。总之，现在已经无话可说了，除了谢谢东京，
That really was astonishing. Anyway,
there's not much else to say now,
except thank you, Tokyo,

846
01:01:23,140 --> 01:01:26,940
谢谢它的空旷，也非常感谢收看。
for being empty and thank you
very much for watching.

847
01:01:26,940 --> 01:01:28,660
下周见，晚安！
See you next week, good night!

848
01:01:28,660 --> 01:01:30,100
欢呼 与 掌声
CHEERS AND APPLAUSE

